  "chain": "Audio Tone trip system cable failure [cause X, under investigation] -> invalid generator lockout (2-50F-386A relay, CB-225/CB-215 open) -> turbine trip -> automatic reactor scram [mitigated by TTR-1 replacement, TTR-2 redundancy]; separately: sealing steam pressure control valve mis-set -> valve fails to admit steam -> condenser vacuum degrades -> level control transferred to RCIC [backups RCIC, HPCI(pressure control only)]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two largely independent failure threads exist in this event: (1) an Audio Tone cable failure causing an invalid generator lockout/scram (root cause code X, still under root-cause investigation), and (2) a separate, unrelated sealing-steam pressure control valve mis-setting that caused condenser vacuum degradation and prompted temporary use of RCIC (and HPCI for pressure control only, not injection). Both are modeled as parallel chains since the narrative treats them as distinct issues with separate corrective actions. HPCI and RCIC are modeled as System nodes (not omitted) because the narrative states they were actively used/operable during the event, not merely described as design context. Previous similar event (2001, EN 38241) modeled as a stub LER per instructions, using the referenced identifier as its key since no formal LER number was given for it."
